Open Vanilla 0022: a spent Star Pouch goes away when you click it.

A Star Pouch is spent when its loot window closes with everything taken (Loot::Release, patch 0005).
When that release was missed, the pouch stayed in the bags with its loot all taken, and every
right-click showed an empty loot window: "I opened the Star Pouch and got the items, but it still
shows I have it, and clicking on it does nothing" (a player's report, 2026-10-21). Opening a pouch
whose loot is all taken now spends it (one from a stack) instead.

diff --git a/src/game/Spells/SpellHandler.cpp b/src/game/Spells/SpellHandler.cpp
index de931cc..eaeab50 100644
--- a/src/game/Spells/SpellHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/game/Spells/SpellHandler.cpp
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 #include "Spells/SpellAuras.h"
 #include "Loot/LootMgr.h"
 #include "OpenVanilla/Play.h"
+#include "OpenVanilla/StarPouch.h"
 
 void WorldSession::HandleUseItemOpcode(WorldPacket& recvPacket)
 {
@@ -246,6 +247,20 @@ void WorldSession::HandleOpenItemOpcode(WorldPacket& recvPacket)
     else
     {
         Loot*& loot = pItem->m_loot;
+
+        // OpenVanilla: a Star Pouch whose loot is all taken is spent. The release that spends it
+        // (Loot::Release, patch 0005) can be missed, and then every click showed an empty loot
+        // window: the pouch stayed in the bags and "nothing happens" (a player's report, 2026-10-21).
+        if (loot && StarPouch::IsPouch(pItem->GetEntry()) && loot->IsLootedFor(pUser))
+        {
+            uint32 one = 1;
+            if (pItem->GetCount() > 1)
+                pUser->DestroyItemCount(*pItem, one, true);
+            else
+                pUser->DestroyItem(pItem->GetBagSlot(), pItem->GetSlot(), true);
+            return;
+        }
+
         if (!loot)
             loot = new Loot(pUser, pItem, LOOT_PICKPOCKETING);
 
